ness and team. \n\nNow get the recognition you deserve.\n\nAbout the awards2026 WinnersCategory & eligibilityNomination processJudging criteriaFAQ\nAbout the Awards\n\nThe SME AI Impact Awards celebrate and recognise SMEs that have achieved business benefits, growth and digital transformation through Al. This award, jointly organised by IMDA and SBF, is part of the National AI Impact Programme and is in support of Singapore's National Al Strategy.\n\nThis year, the Awards recognise 30 SMEs who have achieved business impact and results with Al.\n\nSME AI Impact Awards 2026 winners\nMeet the 30 Innovation & Adoption Excellence winners\nINNOVATION EXCELLENCE\n15 WINNERS\nAccountingbpo\nUses AI to cut accounting document processing time by up to 67%\nBusiness Services\nAccountingbpo\nProfessional services firm and business process outsourcing (BPO) provider specialising in tech-enabled financial management, corporate compliance, and digital accounting workflows.\nUp to 67% reduction\nin accounting document processing time\nUp to 16x faster\nmanagement reporting\n396 manhours\nredirected monthly from administrative coordination to client work\nKEY CHALLENGES\nLabour-intensive accounting processes\nManual data entry and reconciliation created heavy administrative work and delayed the timely completion of accounts\nFragmented work coordination\nAssignments and client information were managed across various documents, requiring 400 hours of coordination each month\nLimited ability to scale\nHigher client volumes required more manpower, limiting scalability and margins\nTHE AI SOLUTION\nYi.Suite: AI Accounting Ecosystem\nAn integrated ecosystem of specialised AI solutions built around its accounting workflows\nYi.Suite connects document processing, client requests, reconciliation, financial reporting and analysis in an end-to-end workflow\nAutomated document processing\nUses AI to extract information from invoices and accounting documents, suggest accounts and match vendors, and supports batch or single-document processing\nAI-supported work coordination\nConverts client emails into trackable work tickets, recommends task assignments, drafts context-aware replies and provides workload and status summaries\nAutomated reconciliation and follow-up\nMatches bank transactions against accounting records, drafts receivables follow-up communications and prepares scheduled management reports\nConversational financial analysis\nAllows business owners to ask financial questions in plain language and generates KPI summaries, charts and dashboards from accounting data\nAI-assisted financial statement preparation\nSupports document verification, draft financial statement compilation and cash-flow preparation, with accountants reviewing and approving the outputs\nBest Marketing Agency\nUses AI to automate routine workflows and increase revenue per employee by 71%\nMedia & Creative\nBest Marketing Agency\nProvides digital marketing services including SEO, paid advertising, social media management and content creation services\n71% increase\nin revenue per employee\n73% increase\nin delivery capacity per head\n1,000 staff-hours saved\nfrom routine work per month\nKEY CHALLENGES\nFragmented and manual operations\nClient delivery, reporting, finance and internal operations were spread across separate tools, spreadsheets and chat threads\nTime-consuming administrative work\nAccount managers spent around two working days per client each month preparing reports, while finance and other administrative processes were also handled manually\nRising costs and missed opportunities\nManual coordination contributed to high overheads while taking senior staff away from sales, strategy and client engagement\nTHE AI SOLUTION\nBig Beast: AI-powered Operating System\nConnects and automates client delivery, reporting, finance and internal operations\nBig Beast embeds AI agents across business workflows to execute routine processes, while retaining human approval for consequential actions\nAutomated client reporting\nPulls advertising and SEO data, tracks keyword performance and generates AI-assisted campaign summaries and live reports\nAI-enabled finance workflows\nAutomates invoicing, bank reconciliation and accounting workflows, with human approval for financial actions\nIntegrated business operations\nBrings task management, payroll, CPF computation, HR processes and contract e-signing into one platform\nAI-assisted content and quality control\nDrafts SEO content, advertisements and landing pages, with automated quality and compliance checks supporting human review\nAutomated client and lead management\nRoutes leads to relevant teams, flags unanswered enquiries and identifies renewal risks using campaign and payment records\nBlue Aqua International\nUses AI to improve feed efficiency by around 30%\nAquaculture\nBlue Aqua International\nProvides sustainable aquaculture, animal nutrition and farm management solutions to farmers worldwide\n30% improvement\nin managing production cost\n6–9 % higher\nsurvival rates\nAround 2,500 manpower\nhours saved annually\nKEY CHALLENGES\nLimited visibility of farm conditions\nInfrequent water quality checks meant issues could go undetected between readings, increasing the risk of losses\nReactive feeding and disease management\nGeneric feeding led to inefficient feed use and spending, while late disease detection increased the risk of stock losses\nFragmented decision-making\nFarm decisions relied heavily on individual experience, paper logs and inconsistent records, making performance difficult to compare across farms\nTHE AI SOLUTION\nAquaPilot: AI-driven Aquaculture Intelligence Platform\nPredicts farm risks and recommends actions using real-time aquaculture data\nAquaPilot analyses water quality, feeding, health and production data to translate Blue Aqua's aquaculture expertise into consistent, data-driven farm decisions\nPredictive water quality management\nAnalyses sensor and farm data to forecast oxygen, ammonia and temperature 6 to 24 hours ahead and alert teams to potential issues\nAI-enabled disease risk detection\nGenerates daily pond-level risk scores and flags potential health issues 4 to 7 days before they typically become visible\nAI-powered feed optimisation\nCalculates daily feed requirements for each pond based on biomass, water conditions, growth patterns and health risks\nAI-assisted system management\nMonitors the Recirculating Aquaculture System to predict potential issues and adjust feeding accordingly\nData-driven farm intelligence\nBenchmarks ponds on feed conversion, survival, growth and production cost and provides farm-specific recommendations to increase farm yield\nGetGo Technologies\nUses AI to detect vehicle damage and recovers $20,000 in billings\nTransport & Mobility\nGetGo Technologies\nProvides on-demand carsharing on a pay-as-you-drive basis\n53% reduction\nin lead time for damage-to-invoices\n60% less\nmanual review workload\nS$20,000 recovered\nin damage costs within two months\nKEY CHALLENGES\nImpractical manual screening\nAround 7,000 daily bookings generate about 56,000 end-trip photos, making it impractical to manually inspect every booking for damage\nDelayed damage detection\nVehicle damage could go unnoticed until reported by users or discovered during workshop inspection days or weeks later\nDifficulty recovering damage costs\nLate detection made it difficult to attribute damage to the responsible booking, resulting in cost of repair that cannot be recovered\nTHE AI SOLUTION\nProject Desmond: AI-powered Vehicle Damage Detection\nAuto detects vehicle damage to reduce damage costs\nCombines computer vision, image matching and human validation to identify vehicle damage, determine when it occurred and support accurate billing\nAI vehicle damage detection\nAnalyses end-trip photos to detect billable damage such as scratches, dents, cracks and dangling parts\nBooking-level damage attribution\nCompares consecutive bookings to determine when damage first appeared and link it to the relevant booking\nAI-powered image matching\nUses image embeddings to determine whether detected damage is new or recurring across adjacent bookings\nHuman-validated damage workflow\nRoutes AI-flagged cases to human reviewers for validation before confirmed cases proceed for follow-up and billing\nContinuous AI model improvement\nRetrains the model using real-world failure cases such as rain and reflections to improve precision and reduce false positives\nGlints Singapore\nUses AI to speed up internal knowledge searches by around 90%\nTalent & Recruitment\nGlints Singapore\nProvides talent and managed workforce services across Singapore, Malaysia, Indonesia, Vietnam, the Philippines and Taiwan.\n90% reduction\nin time spent fact-finding\n1,700 specialist hours\nsaved in six months\nS$120,000 worth\nof staff time saved a year\nKEY CHALLENGES\nFragmented company knowledge\nCritical information was spread across databases, business systems and employment laws in six different markets\nSlow responses to queries\nRoutine questions often required help from Finance, Engineering or other specialists, with complex queries taking hours or days\nOperational and compliance risks\nRepeated queries distracted specialists from their work, while inconsistent answers created regulatory risks across different markets\nTHE AI SOLUTION\nGlimmer: Knowledge Mining AI Agent\nConnects company data and knowledge to help employees answer customers’ questions\nGlimmer lets employees ask questions in plain language and retrieves answers from company systems, internal knowledge, source code and employment laws\nUnified AI knowledge assistant\nAnswers questions in plain language using company data and internal knowledge, with supporting sources shown\nReal-time enterprise data retrieval\nRetrieves up-to-date client, employee, invoice and billing information from systems such as NetSuite and HubSpot\nAI-enabled technical support\nReads the company&apos;s source code to answer platform questions and provide first-line support before unresolved issues are escalated\nBuilt-in accuracy and governance\nSystem automatically flags missing information, restricts citations to accessed sources and maintains audit logs\nGreenphyto\nUses AI to improve crop inspection time by 10X\nAgriculture\nGreenphyto\nOperates a high-density indoor vertical farm for large-scale crop production\n10x faster\nin crop inspection time\nUp to 150x\nproductivity improvement\n90% crop yield\nconsistency\nKEY CHALLENGES\nLate detection of crop issues\nPlant defects and abnormal growth are not detected timely for intervention\nManual inspections\nCrop and equipment checks relied heavily on people and multiple systems\nChallenging yield forecasting\nLimited continuous crop measurements made harvest planning difficult\nTHE AI SOLUTION\nAI-powered Farm Operations Management System (FOMS™)\nConnects farm data, images, sensors and workflows into one system\nUses AI to support decisions and improve production efficiency, moving farm operations from manual monitoring to a continuous, data-driven model.\nEarly defect detection\nDetects crop growth issues, defects and abnormalities earlier using computer vision for early intervention\nFaster inspections\nReplaces many manual crop checks with AI-powered image checks\nMore accurate harvest planning\nImproves yield forecasting by analysing farm data with AI\nLess manual intervention\nIntegrates farm systems, sensors and workflows to reduce manual work\nReal-time alerts\nFlags issues such as lighting or device problems for timely follow-up\niAPPS Health Group\nUses AI to help doctors manage up to four times more patients\nHealthcare\niAPPS Health Group\nProvides primary care, preventive health and diagnostic services supported by proprietary digital health infrastructure\nUp to 4x increase\nin doctor productivity\nUp to 10x increase\nin health coach productivity\nUp to 4x revenue growth\nacross AI-enabled clinics\nKEY CHALLENGES\nManpower-intensive operations\nPharmacy, claims and finance processes required significant administrative resources as clinic operations grew\nFragmented and reactive care\nPatient records, pharmacy, claims, finance and workforce management were spread across isolated systems\nDifficult to scale consistently\nUneven workload and limited decision support made it difficult to expand while maintaining consistent care quality\nTHE AI SOLUTION\n1docAI: AI-native Healthcare Operating System\nIntegrates AI across patient care, clinical decisions and healthcare operations\n1docAI connects six AI domains across patient care, clinical decision-making, health coaching, pharmacy, enterprise operations and payments\nAI-enabled patient management\nCoordinates appointments, live queues and follow-ups to support patient flow and continuity of care\nAI-assisted clinical decision support\nRetrieves source-linked clinical evidence, supports diagnostic reasoning and applies safety checks, with final decisions made by doctors\nPersonalised health coaching\nUses longitudinal health data and behavioural intelligence to provide personalised, real-time coaching between consultations\nAutomated pharmacy and enterprise operations\nAutomates dispensing, inventory, claims, finance, reconciliation, HR and workforce rostering\nIntegrated healthcare and payments\nConnects clinical, operational and payment workflows through a shared longitudinal data record\nKyanon Digital\nUses AI to cut new AI project setup time by 83%\nICT/Consultancy\nKyanon Digital\nDigital technology company and agile software development firm specialising in end-to-end digital transformation, data analytics, and enterprise IT solutions.\n83% reduction\nin setup time for new AI engagements\n80x faster\nbusiness-rule changes\n75% increase\nin concurrent AI delivery capacity\nKEY CHALLENGES\nRepetitive & long lead time for development work\nTeams had to rebuild common capabilities for orchestral, retrieval, integrations, AI evaluation and monitoring before client-specific development could begin\nHeavy reliance on AI engineers\nBusiness-rules were embedded in application code with routine rule changes requiring around five working days of engineering effort, while AI quality checks also relied heavily on manual review\nLimited planning flexibility\nThe company could support around four concurrent AI engagements without adding senior AI engineers at a similar rate, limiting its ability to grow efficiently even as demand increased\nTHE AI SOLUTION\nWisdomMind: Enterprise AI Platform\nStandardises core AI capabilities, business rules, integrations and quality controls for faster deployment\nWisdomMind allows teams to start from a governed production framework and adapt it to each client engagement\nReusable AI foundation\nShared capabilities for AI-agent orchestration, retrieval, integrations and deployment, allowing new engagements to start from proven platform capabilities instead of building from scratch\nGoverned business-rule management\nSeparates business rules from application code, allowing authorised teams to update rules directly while evaluation, versioning and approval controls are applied before changes reach production\nAutomated AI quality evaluation\nTests AI changes against defined ground-truth scenarios and business rules before deployment, helping teams identify regressions consistently\nReusable enterprise integrations\nProvides shared integration and tool interfaces that can be built once and reused across AI agents and client engagements\nEnd-to-end AI monitoring\nTracks AI execution, latency, errors and inference costs, giving teams visibility to diagnose issues and optimise production workloads\nLimteh Project\nUses AI to reduce 80% rework on orders\nRetail\nLimteh Project\nCreates customised corporate gifts, gift sets and personalised presents\n80% less\nrework on orders\nMore than 20 hours\nsaved each week\nUp to $5,800\nsaved monthly\nKEY CHALLENGES\nComplex personalised orders\nPersonalisation details from customers through order notes, customer chats and messages in different languages\nLabour-intensive order processing\nStaff manually process around 2,500 orders each month, creating a daily production bottleneck\nCostly errors\nOrder mistakes resulted in reprints, reshipping, wasted materials and unhappy customers\nTHE AI SOLUTION\nMilo: AI-powered Order Automation\nAutomates personalised orders from sales to production\nMilo interprets customer orders and prepares production instructions, while AI verification helps improve accuracy and flags uncertain orders for review\nAI order interpretation\nReads orders and chats across marketplaces to identify each customer’s personalisation requirements\nAutomated production preparation\nTurns customer requirements into production instructions and automates print-file preparation\nAI-powered verification\nCross-checks order details and flags uncertainties for staff review\nContinuous improvement\nLearns from staff corrections to improve order processing over time\nBusiness and marketing automation\nAutomates sales reporting, stock alerts, profit-and-loss dashboards and creation of marketing content\nLithan Academy\nUses AI to cut curriculum development time by 75%\nEducation\nLithan Academy\nProvides adult education to bridge AI skills for a productive workforce\n75% faster\ncurriculum development\n60% less\nmanual monitoring and support\nAbout 60%\nyear-on-year revenue growth\nKEY CHALLENGES\nLengthy curriculum development\nA 60-hour module required around 300 staff hours to map competencies, prepare content, assessments and rubrics\nDifficulty scaling personalised learner support\nLearners progressed at different speeds, while limited trainer capacity made it difficult to provide timely, customised support\nDelayed learner intervention\nAttendance, assignments and programme progress tracked separately, making it harder to spot learner issues in-time.\nTHE AI SOLUTION\nAdaptive CLaaS: AI-powered Personalised Learning System\nReduces curriculum work and extends personalised support beyond trainer capacity\nComprises three integrated modules: CLaaS Developer for curriculum development, CLaaS Mentor for personalised learner experience and CLaaS Manager for learner monitoring & management\nAI-assisted curriculum development\nCLaaS Developer uses generative AI to create first drafts of learning pathways, session plans, content and assessments, with AI-assisted quality checks and curriculum teams reviewing and refining outputs\nAdaptive personalised learning\nCLaaS Mentor adjusts learning pace and difficulty based on learner progress and recommends resources for identified gaps\nAI-powered learner support\nProvides on-demand guidance, reminders and automated assessment feedback, while escalating learners that need more support\nData-driven learner management\nCLaaS Manager consolidates enrolment, attendance, assignment completion and programme progress into a 360 view\nHuman-in-the-loop learning delivery\nAI handles repetitive curriculum development and routine learner guidance, while curriculum teams and trainers retain responsibility for content quality and complex interventions\nMencast Marine\nUses AI to generate $900,000 in new revenue\nMarine and Offshore Energy\nMencast Marine\nProvides marine propulsion design, manufacturing and repair for the global marine and offshore industry\n50% faster\ndesign turnaround\n75% higher\nproductivity for knowledge-intensive tasks\n$900,000 new\nrevenue within 18 months\nKEY CHALLENGES\nTime-consuming design process\nConventional methods restrict the number of options engineers could evaluate, slowing complex projects\nPressure to lower design costs\nGrowing competition from lower-cost players reduced margins and placed pressure on Mencast's design-led business\nLabour-intensive and manual operations\nLengthy production cycles and manual information retrieval slowed quotations, workflows and operational efficiency\nTHE AI SOLUTION\nMencast AI Platform (MAIP)\nUses AI to enhance propulsion design, manufacturing and operational workflows\nMAIP combines AI, computer vision and enterprise knowledge automation to improve productivity, streamline workflows and centralise data access\nAI-powered propulsion design\nAnalyses thousands of design possibilities to identify higher-performing options and shorten the design process\nDesign differentiation\nLeverages decades of engineering and sea-trial data to develop differentiated propulsion solutions beyond competing primarily on price\nIntelligent manufacturing optimisation\nCombines AI, computer vision and sensors to improve quality and support more efficient production\nEnterprise knowledge automation\nOrganises enterprise knowledge and automates workflows such as quotations, claims processing, research and information retrieval\nOceanus Media Global\nUses AI to cut production timelines by around 80%\nMedia & Creative\nOceanus Media Global\nCreative media technology company specialising in virtual production, generative AI, content production, distribution and IP licensing\n80% shorter\nproduction timelines\nUp to 85% lower\nproduction costs\n200% increase\nin multi-location project capacity\nKEY CHALLENGES\nLong production timelines\nMulti-location productions could take 14-15 weeks due to location scouting, permits, travel, set construction and filming\nHigh production costs\nLocation fees, permits, travel, transport and set construction increased  production costs significantly\nLimited production capacity\nCrews and equipment were largely committed to one major production at a time, limiting the number of projects the company could take on concurrently\nTHE AI SOLUTION\nAI-integrated Virtual Production Pipeline\nCreates multiple locations virtually for faster, more efficient media production\nCombines generative AI, computer vision and AI agents across pre-production, filming, post-production and localisation, with creative control retained by the team\nAI-assisted pre-production\nSupports script breakdown, scene planning, scheduling, storyboarding and visualisation before filming\nAI-generated virtual environments\nCreates digital environments and reconstructs real locations as virtual sets for filming in a controlled studio\nAI-enabled filming\nFilms actors against AI-built virtual environments, with real-time camera tracking maintaining correct perspective\nAI-supported visual effects\nAutomates repetitive editing tasks and supports the creation of visual-effects elements\nAI-powered localisation and versioning\nSupports dubbing in four languages and adapts approved content for different formats and platforms\nONG&ONG Group\nUses AI to cut workflow durations by up to 95%\nBuilt Environment\nONG&ONG Group\nProvides built environment consultancy services across Asia, integrating architectural practice, urban master planning, landscape design, interior design and project management with comprehensive civil, structural, mechanical and electrical engineering\nUp to 95% savings\nin workflow duration\n22,500 professional hours\nestimated to be recovered annually\nApprox. 4x return\non AI investment\nKEY CHALLENGES\nTime-consuming information retrieval\nUp to 2,750 manhours a week spent searching for project precedents, building regulations, policies and project information scattered across multiple systems\nReliance on staff knowledge\nTechnical expertise sat with experienced staff, while accessing knowledge from past projects required staff to know the exact reference to search for\nLabour-intensive processes\nManual regulatory, design, presentation and financial reporting tasks slowed project delivery and management reporting\nTHE AI SOLUTION\n360i: AI Platform\nConnects the company’s project knowledge, regulatory information and business workflows in a secure and governed environment\n360i enables staff to search institutional knowledge, check regulations, generate project materials and automate selected business processes using AI grounded in the firm's own data and standards.\nAI-powered knowledge retrieval\nAllows staff to search over 12,000 historical projects and internal information using plain-language questions, with answers linked back to source records\nRegulatory compliance support\nDedicated assistants answer questions on Singapore building regulations and CORENET X requirements, providing citations to relevant source clauses\nAI-assisted design visualisation\nGenerates and edits architectural, interior, urban and landscape concept images, allowing designers to explore multiple directions within hours  \nAI-powered financial reporting and analysis\nConsolidates and validates financial data across 10 entities to produce the Group's P&L, while AI analyst modules generate alerts, forecasts and scenario analyses\nAI-enabled professional workflows\nExtends into PowerPoint, Excel, Outlook and document workflows, while specialised tools support branded presentation creation, exact calculations and landscape research\nSupreme Components International\nUses AI to accelerate RFQ processing, cutting sourcing and quote preparation time by up to 90%\nWholesale Trade\nSupreme Components International\nSupplies active, passive and electromechanical components to original equipment manufacturers and electronic manufacturing companies across tech sectors\nUp to 90% faster\nsourcing and quote preparation\n96% reduction\nin bills of materials preparation time\nUp to $32,000\nin monthly productivity gains\nKEY CHALLENGES\nUnstructured Request For Quotation (RFQ) submissions\nRFQs arrived in multiple formats and increasing volumes, making them difficult to process, track and manage efficiently\nInaccurate and error-prone matching\nManual product and brand matching increased the risk of quoting inaccuracies and cause unnecessary followups\nFragmented supplier information \nSupplier pricing and lead-time information was scattered across emails and records\nTHE AI SOLUTION\nAtlas (AI RFQ-to-Fulfilment Platform)\nUses AI to transform RFQ and supplier data into structured, searchable information\nAutomates RFQ processing and sourcing workflows - help teams improve accuracy, reduce manual effort and respond to customer requests more efficiently\nAI-enabled RFQ processing\nExtracts customer and product requirements from emails, PDFs, spreadsheets and other RFQ formats into structured data\nIntelligent product matching\nMatches requested products and brands against supplier information to streamline sourcing and quotation workflows\nSupplier intelligence and sourcing\nExtracts supplier prices, inventory and lead times from emails while identifying stock availability, supplier options and product alternatives\nAutomated RFQ workflow\nCentralises RFQ and supplier information while automating supplier outreach, making information easier to search, track and reuse\nThriving Weeds\nUses AI to enable continuous waste monitoring with more than 95% accuracy in waste weight measurements\nEnvironmental Services\nThriving Weeds\nProvides waste audits, data analysis and sustainability consultancy to help organisations improve resource and waste management\n60% fewer\nflagged contamination incidents\n>95%\ndata accuracy\nUp to 384 manhours\nsaved per audit\nKEY CHALLENGES\nManpower-intensive waste audits\nConventional audits could involve 6-8 people collecting and sorting waste for up to 12 hours a day\nLimited visibility between audits\nShort manual sampling periods made it difficult to identify daily variations, repeated contamination and longer-term waste patterns\nManual process limited scalability\nRepeated on-site audits and lengthy reporting required significant time and resources for each premise\nTHE AI SOLUTION\nAuditEye Waste-to-Cloud Ecosystem\nCombines AI, IoT and cloud technology for continuous waste monitoring\nAuditEye captures and structures waste data over longer periods, while retaining human verification and professional consultancy for waste-reduction recommendations\nContinuous monitoring\nCaptures disposal records throughout the deployment period to provide a larger and more representative dataset\nAI-enabled contaminant detection\nIdentifies contaminants in waste streams and records when contamination occurs, including disposal weight and frequency\nAutomated data capture\nLinks images with weight, time, location and waste-stream information to create standardised records for analysis\nCloud-based intelligence\nProcesses records in near real time and provides access to waste data, images and downloadable records\nHuman-validated analysis\nCombines continuous monitoring with consultant review and physical audits to verify findings and develop recommendations\nView all winners\nADOPTION EXCELLENCE\n15 WINNERS\nAgape CP Holdings\nUses AI to cut administration tasks by over 60%\nBusiness Services\nAgape CP Holdings\nSocial enterprise providing contact centre, customer experience, business process outsourcing, recruitment and workforce development services\n63% less time\nspent on administrative tasks\n33% faster\nnew-agent onboarding\n16x more\nquality assurance coverage\nKEY CHALLENGES\nTime-consuming post-call administration\nAgents spent 3-5 minutes documenting each interaction and updating records, reducing time available to serve customers\nLimited service-quality visibility\nSupervisors could only review 5% of interactions, limiting their ability to identify service gaps, compliance risks and coaching opportunities\nSlow onboarding\nNew agents could take around six weeks to reach independent productivity, with some requiring additional knowledge support and initial-deployment coaching\nTHE AI SOLUTION\nAI-powered Contact Centre and BPO Platform\nSupports customer service, quality monitoring and workforce productivity with AI\nCombines generative AI, speech analytics and workflow automation to support agents and supervisors acros