\nClaude assists with research, strategy development, content drafting and client communications\nAI-assisted creative production\nHiggsfield generates AI video assets while AdCreative.ai generates advertising creatives\nStandardised business communications\nBlip AI helps employees with routine written communications across departments\nCatalyst Performance\nUses AI to improve organic search clicks by over 300%\nPersonal Care Services\nCatalyst Performance\nSpecialises in assessment-led fitness coaching and long-term health optimisation through personal training and wellness\nOver 300% increase\nin organic search clicks\n190% increase\nin search impressions\nMore than 2X improvement\nin Google search ranking\nKEY CHALLENGES\nLimited online visibility\nThe legacy website lacked SEO and GEO infrastructure, limiting organic discoverability\nManual and resource-intensive marketing\nWebsite updates, content creation, advertising campaigns and lead outreach required significant time or external agency support\nLimited in-house digital capacity\nThe website, marketing systems and operational tools required significant time or external agency support\nTHE AI SOLUTION\nAI-powered Digital Operations\nBuilds and manages digital capabilities that would otherwise require external agencies or dedicated technical staff\nEmbeds Claude across website, marketing and operational workflows\nAI-built website and search optimisation\nRebuilt the website with SEO and GEO infrastructure to improve visibility across Google and AI search engines\nAutomated outreach and lead nurturing\nPowers LinkedIn outreach, automated email campaigns and personalised follow-ups to convert leads\nAI-powered advertising analysis\nAnalyses Meta, Google and TikTok campaign data to identify inefficient ad spend and improve allocation\nAI-operated dashboards\nBuilt dashboards that provide visibility on bookings, leads, protocol sales, email performance and funnel analytics\nGOODSTUPH\nUses AI to cut campaign production from four weeks to seven days\nMedia & Creative\nGOODSTUPH\nProvides creative media social marketing services\nMore than 30%\ncost savings\nUp to 4X faster\nproduction turnaround\nOver 200% increase\nin creative output\nKEY CHALLENGES\nHigh outsourced production costs\nExternal shoots, studios and post-production accounted for roughly 60% of total expenses in H1 2025\nLong production cycles\nExternal production added 2-4 weeks to a typical campaign, while changes could add another 3-5 days\nLimited experimentation and client reach\nHigh production costs limit the number of concepts the agency could test and made some lower-budget briefs uneconomical to serve\nTHE AI SOLUTION\nAI.YAH: Generative-AI Creative Production System\nCombines large language models, image generation and generative video within a structured creative workflow\nAI accelerates ideation and production, while human creatives direct the process, evaluate outputs and retain final creative approval\nAI-assisted ideation and scripting\nUses large language models to develop creative concepts and scripts, helping teams explore and develop ideas faster\nGenerative image and video production\nProduces images, videos and creative variations in-house, reducing reliance on external shoots and post-production\nStructured AI creative workflows\nUses role-based prompt frameworks that guide outputs against defined creative and quality standards\nHuman-led creative control\nHuman creatives direct the process, evaluate AI-generated outputs and retain final judgement over what is good enough to release\niHub Solutions\nUses AI to halve the time needed to handle data requests\nLogistics\niHub Solutions\nProvides technology-enabled logistics solutions, including smart warehousing, e-commerce fulfilment and last-mile delivery services\n$94,500\nin projected annual cost savings\n60% less time\nhandling data requests\n15 hours saved\nper day\nKEY CHALLENGES\nLabour-intensive report preparation\nAd hoc data requests required manual extraction, manipulation and report creation beyond standard system reports\nDependence on technical expertise\nComplex requests required software developers to write SQL queries and retrieve information from underlying databases\nHigh query-handling workload\nCustomer service and software development teams spent approximately 25 employee-hours daily responding to reporting and data requests\nTHE AI SOLUTION\nGideon: GenAI Virtual Assistant\nUses natural-language conversations to make warehouse and delivery data more accessible\nEnables customers and employees to retrieve, analyse and explore operational data without requiring technical knowledge or developer support\nNatural-language data queries\nAllows users to ask questions in plain language instead of searching reports or understanding database structures\nAutomated data retrieval\nConverts user requests into SQL queries and retrieves data directly from iHub's Warehouse Management System\nInteractive data analysis\nGenerates charts, refines queries through conversations and presents results in an easy-to-understand format\nSelf-service analytics\nEmpowers customers and non-technical employees to independently access operational insights without relying on technical teams\nInnovative Hub (SG)\nUses AI to cut proposal drafting time by around 80%\nMedia & Creative\nInnovative Hub (SG)\nOffers digital marketing and e-commerce services to clients across Singapore, Malaysia and Vietnam\n2x higher\nemployee productivity\n75% faster\ncustomer response times\n80% faster\nproposal creation\nKEY CHALLENGES\nManual and time-intensive work\nProposal drafting and compliance checks required significant manual effort\nSlow customer response and content delivery\nCustomer response and content translations were dependent on specialist availability and limited by time zones\nLimited scalability\nBusiness growth depended on hiring more staff to handle increasing workload\nTHE AI SOLUTION\nAI-powered Workflow Automation\nLeverages AI tools like Claude, ChatGPT and OpenMax across daily workflows\nUsing AI tools to automate routine tasks, retrieve data and respond to clients quickly.\nFaster proposal creation\nReduces proposal turnaround time from a full day to just a few hours\nMultilingual support\nCompletes content localisation and translations within the same day\nAutomated compliance\nStreamlines audits, checklists and sensitive-word checks \nCross-platform task support\nSupports multi-step tasks completion by working across messaging platforms, spreadsheets, and internal databases\nBroader workflow automation\nSupports prospecting, HR triage, morning briefings, reporting, client monitoring and other routine tasks\nIYLA Collective\nUses AI to increase content output by 4x\nRetail\nIYLA Collective\nDistributes clean and certified-organic beauty and family care products through e-commerce marketplaces and retail channels\nMore than $14,000 saved\nin annual recurring labour\nUp to 4x increase\nin content output\n60 manhours\nper month freed from content production\nKEY CHALLENGES\nTime-consuming content and marketing production\nArticle research, writing and email campaign creation required significant manual effort, restricting output and marketing reach\nLabour-intensive sales analysis\nSales data from multiple platforms had to be consolidated and reconciled manually, delaying pricing and inventory decisions\nLimited capacity for product development\nMobile app development was costly and relied on external vendors\nTHE AI SOLUTION\nAI-powered Operations Solution\nUses AI to automate content, marketing, analytics and software development workflows\nIYLA embedded Claude, Grok and Claude Code across the business to expand operating capacity and reduce reliance on external resources\nContent creation support\nResearches, drafts and localises educational content and product information across multiple brands\nMarketing automation\nBuilds and refines email campaigns and customer journeys, enabling more campaigns to be produced with the same team\nAI-assisted sales analytics\nAnalyses and reconciles sales across multiple marketplaces, providing faster insights for pricing and inventory decisions\nIn-house app development\nUses AI-assisted coding tools to build customer-facing digital products without relying on external agencies\nKopi Near Me\nUses AI to cut technician scheduling time by 80%\nFood & Beverage\nKopi Near Me\nOperates a network of automated coffee vending machines across commercial, healthcare and transport locations in Singapore\nUp to 15% increase\nin sales conversion\n70% reduction\nin manual enquiry processing\n80% less time\non technician scheduling\nKEY CHALLENGES\nFragmented sales and contract processes\nCustomer requirements arrived through multiple communication channels, requiring staff to manually extract information and prepare sales documents\nComplex field operations scheduling\nManaging replenishment, maintenance and repairs across machines required extensive coordination of technicians, routes and operational priorities\nFragmented operational data\nInventory, logistics and operational records were spread across multiple systems and spreadsheets, resulting in significant manual data entry and limited visibility\nTHE AI SOLUTION\nAI-enabled Operating System\nAutomates sales, scheduling and operational workflows across the business\nThe integrated platform streamlines customer onboarding, optimises field operations and provides real-time operational visibility\nSales process automation\nExtracts customer requirements from enquiries and converts them into structured sales orders, quotations and contracts\nDynamic scheduling and routing\nOptimises replenishment, maintenance and repair schedules while adjusting technician deployment based on operational needs\nCentralised operations management\nManages inventory, logistics and operational records through a unified platform, reducing manual administration\nReal-time operational visibility\nProvides management dashboards and live operational insights to support planning and decision-making\nLil' but Mighty Education Centre\nUses AI to cut personalised parent communication preparation time by over 80%\nEducation\nLil' but Mighty Education Centre\nProvides English enrichment for primary and secondary school students with its proprietary curriculum\n300% increase\nin marketing output\nUp to 83% reduction\nin parent communication turnaround time\nOver 6,200 hours\nsaved yearly on repetitive tasks\nKEY CHALLENGES\nLabour-intensive content creation\nLesson materials, marketing campaigns and parent communications required significant manual effort, slowing turnaround and limiting output\nManual internal documentation\nStaff training materials, SOPs, performance-management documents and internal reports required significant time to prepare and maintain\nFragmented organisational knowledge\nExpertise and information remained distributed across individuals, resulting in duplicated work, inconsistent documentation and repeated coordination\nTHE AI SOLUTION\nAI-powered Curriculum, Content and Operations\nStreamlines repetitive work and improves organisational efficiency\nEmbeds AI across curriculum development, marketing and operational workflows\nAI-enhanced curriculum development\nAccelerates lesson planning, assessment creation and development of teaching resources, with educators reviewing and refining AI-generated materials\nAI-assisted content and communications\nCreates first drafts of marketing content, webinar materials, website content and parent communications\nAutomated administrative workflows\nUses AI and connected automation tools to streamline repetitive processes, consolidate information and reduce manual coordination across departments\nAI-assisted internal documentation\nHelps create and maintain staff training materials, SOPs and performance-management documents\nKnowledge management\nOrganises tasks, prioritises information and improves access to organisational knowledge\nLinksworkz Design Studio\nUses AI to cut proposal preparation tasks time\nBuilt Environment\nLinksworkz Design Studio\nProvides signage, wayfinding and environmental graphics consultancy services for hotels, commercial developments and transportation facilities\n1300% Return on Investment\n(ROI) within the first year\n$60,000\nin annual manpower savings\n70% faster\nproposal preparation\nKEY CHALLENGES\nTime-consuming proposal preparation\nClient briefs, Request for Proposals (RFPs) and drawings required extensive review before customised proposals could be developed, consuming significant senior leadership time\nLabour-intensive project research\nLocation, cultural and user-journey research required around three working days of analysis before concept development could begin\nHigh operational and documentation workload\nMeeting records, project documentation and coordination tasks consumed significant staff time and created bottlenecks across concurrent projects\nTHE AI SOLUTION\nAI Assistants and Semi-Automated Workflows\nUses company-specific AI assistants to support business development, project research and operational workflows\nThe AI assistants handle first-stage reading, organisation and drafting, allowing staff to focus on design thinking, client engagement and quality control.\nProposal development support\nReviews client briefs, RFPs and drawings to identify project scope, deliverables, risks and information required for fee preparation\nProject research and wayfinding\nSupports research, user-journey analysis, signage planning and information organisation using Linksworkz's methods and expertise\nStreamlined operations and documentation\nAssists with contract reviews, meeting summaries, project documentation and access to company procedures and standards\nDesign exploration\nSupports early-stage concept development by exploring visual directions, materials and design options for client presentations\nHuman-led review\nKeeps design decisions, technical accuracy and final approvals under the responsibility of experienced staff\nMcLink Asia\nUses AI to increase campaign production capacity by 200%\nICT/Consultancy\nMcLink Asia\nProvides office equipment, enterprise software integration and managed IT services to businesses in Singapore and Asia\n200% increase\nin campaign production capacity\n95% faster\nresponse to customers\n85% faster\ncampaign roll-out\nKEY CHALLENGES\nSlow to respond to customers\nStaff took hours or days to respond to social media enquiries\nLong time taken to deliver campaigns\nA single campaign required 8-12 hours of combined staff effort to deliver\nDelayed campaign launches\nManual revisions and handovers slowed campaign production, limiting the ability to respond quickly to market opportunities\nTHE AI SOLUTION\nMulti-agent AI Marketing Platform\nAutomates marketing from lead qualification to reporting\nSpecialised AI agents work together to qualify leads, create content, prepare campaigns and analyse performance, reducing repetitive work and handovers\nAutomated AI lead qualification\nResponds to social enquiries and helps identify and qualify potential leads\nAI campaign creation\nAI content generation creates blogs, newsletters, videos and promotional images quickly and prepares campaigns for distribution\nConnected multi-agent workflow\nAI agents work across campaign tasks, reducing manual handovers and delays\nAutomated marketing analytics\nCollects advertising data and prepares performance reports with less manual work\nNami Japanese Academy\nUses AI to handle scheduling requests, cutting resolution time to under two hours\nEducation\nNami Japanese Academy\nLanguage school specialising in Japanese language instruction and cultural enrichment, with lessons delivered in small-group and digital classroom settings.\nUp to 83% less\ntime spent on administrative tasks\n50% fewer\nno-shows\n100% on-time\npayment\nKEY CHALLENGES\nTime-consuming administrative work\nTwo administrators spent around 60 hours each week managing messages, schedules and reminders, reducing time available for other work\nSlow responses to rescheduling requests\nManual coordination between students and teachers meant requests took 3-8 hours to resolve, with after-hours requests delayed until staff were available\nMissed lessons and delayed payments\nInconsistent reminders contributed to more than 10 no-shows and last-minute cancellations each month, while overdue invoices could go unnoticed for weeks\nTHE AI SOLUTION\nThe Nami Concierge: AI-powered WhatsApp Platform\nAutomates lesson scheduling, communication and routine administration\nThe Nami Concierge uses AI to manage routine WhatsApp enquiries and administrative workflows, allowing staff to spend more time towards enhancing teaching quality and student engagement\nAI-powered message handling\nReads and classifies WhatsApp messages and responds to routine requests in the student’s preferred language\nAutomated lesson rescheduling\nChecks live calendars, identifies available slots, coordinates teacher approval and updates bookings automatically\nAutomated reminders and administration\nSends lesson and invoice reminders, marks attendance, generates invoices and extends recurring lesson series\nCentralised conversation management\nProvides staff with a single view of conversations, AI-generated summaries and the ability to take over when needed\nHuman-controlled escalation\nRoutes billing matters, complaints and complex requests to staff for review and action\nThe Gourmet Factor\nUses AI to cut invoice processing time by 80%\nFood & Beverage\nThe Gourmet Factor\nOperates and manages restaurant brands across a range of dining concept\n100% Return on Investment\n(ROI) within five months\n80% faster\ninvoice processing\n40% less\ntime spent on stocktaking\nKEY CHALLENGES\nManual inventory and invoice processing\nStocktaking and supplier invoice processing required significant staff effort, reducing time available for higher-value work\nInventory visibility gaps\nFragmented stock records reduced visibility into inventory levels, contributing to shortages, over-ordering and excess stock\nLimited visibility into food costs and margins\nSupplier pricing data was buried in unprocessed invoices, making it challenging to maintain accurate menu costing and respond to cost increases\nTHE AI SOLUTION\nRestoke.ai: AI-driven Inventory and Back-of-House Platform\nUses AI to automate inventory management, invoice processing and food-cost tracking\nBy connecting supplier pricing, inventory and recipes in a single platform, Restoke.ai provides real-time visibility into stock levels, food costs and margins while reducing manual administration\nAutomated invoice processing\nExtracts supplier invoice details using Optical Character Recognition (OCR) and machine learning, reducing manual data entry and processing effort\nDigital stocktaking\nCaptures inventory counts through mobile devices and synchronises stock information across locations\nReal-time recipe costing\nUpdates recipe costs using live supplier prices, providing greater visibility into menu-item costs and margins\nData-driven purchasing\nUses inventory and costing data to guide purchasing decisions and reduce shortages, over-ordering and excess stock\nTTS Group\nUses AI to increase traffic-data acquisition capacity by about 98%\nTransport & Mobility\nTTS Group\nProvides transport planning, traffic engineering and transport analytics consultancy services.\nAbout 98% increase\nin traffic-data acquisition capacity\nAbout 30 hours saved\nper engineer each week on manual traffic footage review\nAbout 50x more sites\nprocessed monthly\nKEY CHALLENGES\nLabour-intensive traffic data collection\nSurveyors manually counted and classified vehicles and pedestrians, requiring multiple personnel and extended shifts for high-volume sites\nTime-consuming safety analysis\nEngineers spent around 15 hours per week reviewing footage for a single intersection, limiting the number of sites that could be assessed\nReactive road-safety assessment\nPeriodic observations and historical crash data made it difficult to detect near-misses and identify safety risks before incidents occurred\nTHE AI SOLUTION\nTTS Proactive Framework for Near-Miss-Based Traffic Risk Assessment\nUses AI to automate traffic analysis and identify safety risks earlier\nCombines computer vision, predictive analytics and large language models to collect traffic data, detect near-misses and support risk assessment and intervention planning, with engineers retaining responsibility for safety recommendations\nAutomated traffic detection and classification\nDetects, tracks and classifies vehicles and pedestrians using computer vision, reducing reliance on manual traffic counting\nAI-enabled near-miss detection\nAnalyses movement patterns to identify traffic conflicts that may not appear in conventional crash-based assessments\nData-driven risk assessment\nUses traffic and near-miss data to quantify risk and identify higher-risk locations\nAI-assisted intervention planning\nSynthesises data from high-risk intersections to support targeted safety interventions such as signal optimisation\nContinuous post-intervention monitoring\nReassesses sites after interventions to measure changes in safety risk and compare results before and after improvements\nYou Tiao Man\nUses AI to cut supplier invoice processing time by 85%\nFood & Beverage\nYou Tiao Man\nManufactures traditional Asian snacks and frozen dough fritters, supplying hotels, restaurants, caterers and supermarkets\n85% Return on Investment (ROI)\nwithin the first year\n83% less time\nprocessing invoices\n40 manhours\nsaved per week\nKEY CHALLENGES\nFragmented order management\nOrders arrived through multiple sales channels, requiring staff to manually capture and consolidate information across systems\nLabour-intensive invoice processing\nSupplier invoices had to be manually entered, validated and reconciled across spreadsheets and finance systems\n Time-consuming administrative work\nManual payment tracking, follow-up activities and repetitive order administration reduced time available for business development and customer engagement\nTHE AI SOLUTION\nAI Operations Co-Pilot\nUses AI to automate order, finance and marketing workflows while keeping staff in control of approvals\nBuilt using n8n and Claude, the solution integrates with existing business systems to reduce manual processing, improve visibility and streamline day-to-day operations\nAI-assisted invoice processing\nExtracts invoice details, validates pricing against master records and flags discrepancies for staff review\nAutomated finance workflows\nMaintains payment records and transfers approved invoice information into finance systems, reducing duplicate data entry and reconciliation work\nMulti-channel order visibility\nConsolidates orders across sales channels into a live dashboard, providing a unified view of revenue, orders and outstanding actions\nAI-assisted marketing\nResearches and drafts social media content, checks it against company policies and routes posts for approval before publication\nView all winners\nAward categories\nSME Innovation Excellence Award\nSMEs who have developed a proprietary AI solution and successfully deployed it within their own business\nSME Adoption Excellence Award\nSMEs who have successfully implemented ready-to-use or off-the-shelf AI solutions\nEligibility criteria\n\nSMEs who submit nominations must meet the following eligibility requirements:\n\nSingapore-registered company with local operations\nAt least 30% local shareholding\nGroup annual sales turnover below S$100 million, OR group employment size below 200\nMinimum 6 months of AI solution deployment with positive business impact\nNomination process\n\n4 steps to nominate your company for the SME AI Impact Awards — from submitting key company information to celebrating at the Awards ceremony on 13 Oct 2026.\n\nNomination for 2026 closed on 14 August.\n\n \nSubmit key information\n\nStart your nomination process and proceed to submit key information about your company.\n\n \nGet notified\n\nSMEs will receive an email with a unique link to continue the application process.\n\nAll submissions need to be received by 14 Aug 2026.\n\n \nJudging and site visits\n\nNominations will be evaluated and judged.\n\nAs part of the judging validation, site visits will be conducted to observe the use of AI in the business.\n\nAttend the Awards ceremony\n\nAttend the SME AI Impact Awards ceremony on 13 Oct 2026 at SMEs Go Digital Day.\n\nWinners will receive the award on stage.\n\nJudging panel\nMr. Ng Cher Pong\nCE, IMDA\nMr. Kok Ping Soon\nCEO, SBF\nMr. Loh Hean-Ho\nMD & Senior Partner, BCG\nMr. Liew Nam Soon\nSingapore and Asean Managing Partner, EY\nMr. Ben King\nCountry MD Singapore, Google\nMr. Chia Wee Luen\nMD Singapore, Microsoft\nMr. Oliver Jay\nMD International, OpenAI\nJudging criteria\n\nThe SME AI Impact Awards assess the impact of AI on your business. Nominations are evaluated based on the following criteria:\n\nImpact and value add of AI\n\nBusiness problem definition\n\nDescribe the specific business challenge your company faced.\n\nHow significant was the impact of the business challenge on the business?\n\nEffectiveness of solution\n\nHow did the AI solution address the problem?\n\nMeasurable results\n\nProductivity gains\n\nWhat measurable improvements were seen in key business performance metrics?\n\nFinancial impact\n\nWhat financial benefits were achieved as a result of implementing the AI solution?\n\nOperational benefits\n\nDid your business achieve benefits in operations?\n\nChange management and workforce impact\n\nStaff training\n\nHow did your company train staff to ensure successful, ongoing usage of the AI solution in daily operations?\n\nChange in work processes\n\nHow has the AI solution changed day-to-day work processes?\n\nFuture readiness\n\nWhat are the key learning points and how well-prepared is the company for deeper use of AI?\n\nFrequently asked questions\n\nCan a company apply for both award categories?\n\nNo, a company can only apply for one award category. We recommend selecting the category that best reflects your strongest business impact.\n\nCan I apply if my company received grant support for the AI solution?\n\nYes. The SME AI Impact Awards is open to all SMEs who have adopted AI solutions, regardless of government programme participation or grant support. All SMEs are evaluated equally regardless of solution type or grant support received\n\nCan a company apply if the AI solution was developed by a third-party vendor?\n\nYes. The SME AI Impact Awards recognises the business transformation achieved through the use of AI, regardless of whether the solution was built in-house or developed by an external vendor. What matters is how your company has adopted, integrated and leveraged the AI solution to drive measurable impact.\n\nDo IMDA pre-approved AI solutions have any advantage during judging?\n\nNo. All SMEs are evaluated equally regardless of solution type or grant support.\n\nCan a subsidiary of a larger company apply?\n\nA subsidiary may still apply if it meets all of the following eligibility requirements:\nBe registered and operating in Singapore.\nHave at least 30% local shareholding.\nHave a group annual sales turnover not exceeding S$100 million OR a group employment size not exceeding 200 employees.\nHave used an AI solution for a minimum of 6 months with positive business impact.\n\nWhat if my company uses multiple AI solutions?\n\nYou are welcome to highlight multiple AI solutions in your nomination. However, we encourage you to focus on one solution that has delivered the most significant and measurable business impact.\n\nAs an AI solution vendor, can I submit a nomination on behalf of my SME customers?\n\nAll nominations should come directly from SME end users. If you're a vendor or AI solution provider, you could invite your SME customers to submit their nominations.\n\nWhat is the closing date of the nomination period?\n\nThe nomination will be open until the 14th August 2026, 2359hrs.\n\nWhen does the 6 months of solution deployment start and end?\n\nYour company must have used the AI solution for at least 6 months from the date your nomination is submitted.\n\nWhat happens after I submit my nomination?\n\nOnce your nomination is submitted, you will receive an acknowledgement of receipt.\n\nYour submission will be reviewed by our assessment team, and we will be in touch if your company is shortlisted for a site visit.\n\nFinal winners will be announced at the Awards ceremony on 13 October 2026. Invitation to attend the Awards ceremony will be sent closer to date. Company representatives must be present in person.\n\nWhat is the purpose of the site visit? Who will conduct the site visit?\n\nThe site visit serves to verify the information provided in your nomination for a first-hand understanding of how your AI solution has been implemented and the tangible impact it has had on your business. Site visits will be conducted by SBF, the co-organiser and may include a walkthrough of your operations, a demonstration of the AI solution, and a discussion with key personnel involved in the implementation or use of the AI solution.\n\nWill I be notified in advance of the site visit?\n\nYes. Shortlisted companies will be notified in advance, and the site visit will be scheduled at a mutually convenient date and time. You will be given sufficient notice to prepare accordingly. Should you need to reschedule, please contact the organising team as early as possible.\n\nWhat should I prepare for the site visit?\n\nTo make the most of your site visit, we recommend preparing the following:\nA brief presentation or overview of your AI solution including a live demonstration of the AI solution, where possible\nSupporting documentation such as performance metrics, KPIs, and data showing measurable business impact\nKey personnel who were involved in the AI implementation (e.g., project leads, operations staff) to speak to the solution's outcomes\nPersonnel who are actively using the AI solution to speak about how they use the AI solution and how their work scope has changed with AI\n\nHow many award winners will there be?\n\nWe will be recognising up to 30 SMEs this year.\n\nIs my nomination information confidential?\n\nAll information disclosed to IMDA will be kept strictly confidential and used primarily for the purpose of evaluating and selecting award winners. Where applicable, selected information may also be used for marketing and publicity purposes including features on our website and media coverage. We will seek your consent before publishing any such materials.\n\nWhat if I still cannot find answers to my question?\n\nYou can email us at sme_ai_awards@imda.gov.sg.\nReport Vulnerability\nContact us\nTerms of Use\nPrivacy Policy\nReach\n© 2026, Infocomm Media Development Authority. Last Updated 16 Oct 2026"
